# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# gcloud falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, which would work
# but would also upload apps/web (175 MB of node_modules and frontend source)
# that the API image never copies. Being explicit keeps the upload near 40 MB
# and every build noticeably faster.
#
# The Dockerfile needs exactly: pyproject.toml, packages/, apps/api/, scripts/,
# and data/processed/*.csv — the catalogues it builds the index from.

.git/
.gitignore

# The frontend deploys to Vercel; the API image does not contain it.
apps/web/

# Not needed to build or run the service.
tests/
eval/
docs/
infra/
NOTES.md
README.md

# Large, derived, or not ours to redistribute. data/processed/*.csv IS
# uploaded: scripts/build_index.py needs it at image-build time.
data/raw/

# The index is rebuilt inside the image, but the CALIBRATOR is shipped: fitting
# it does thousands of index searches and took >50 minutes on Cloud Build's
# single-vCPU worker. Two small files (85 KB) instead of a 50-minute build step.
data/artifacts/*
!data/artifacts/calibrator.joblib
!data/artifacts/calibration_report.json

# NOTE: data/processed/interactions/ is deliberately NOT excluded here, even
# though .gitignore does exclude it. The two ignore files answer different
# questions:
#
#   .gitignore    "should this 5.5 MB DDInter-derived table live in a public
#                  repository?"  -> no, it is not ours to redistribute
#   .gcloudignore "does the running service need it?"  -> yes, or the
#                  interaction engine reports itself unavailable
#
# Excluding it here shipped a build where /v1/interactions/status returned
# pairs=0 in production while working locally, because the local checkout had
# the file and the image did not. The image cannot regenerate it either: that
# needs data/raw/ddinter/, which is excluded and much larger.

# Local junk
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
.env
*.bak
out/
stages/
